This project follows Agent Builder. If the `agent-builder` skill is available, invoke it
(`/agent-builder:agent-builder`) before substantive work: it knows the phases, the decision ledger, the seeder and
checker, and the closeout. If it is not installed, this file and `governance/` are sufficient.

At the first response of each coding session, run `python3 scripts/version.py` and
report its notice once. This describes the project's own version, not its template.
Before Build, agree a change budget using `governance/change-budget.md`; run
`python3 scripts/changes.py .` after coherent edits and before commits. Re-estimate
overruns with the author; never compress readable code. Show estimates, Build actuals versus
estimates and final line/code-size totals in chat (green/red diff blocks where supported).
Preserve shared approval; detailed working notes stay local.

Before substantive work, read `governance/operating-agreement.md`,
`governance/project-state.yaml`, and `governance/decisions.yaml` completely. When asked for
status or where things stand, give a briefing — project and purpose, phase and status, what
exists and what does not yet, every decision with ID and status, the next step inside the
phase — not a one-line summary; the reader may be picking this project up cold.

